 uh immediately understanding irony and  metaphor and idioms  for example in this text here  reads  yesterday in a nutshell first it was  raining cats and dogs then got canned  etc so when i'm reading this text  my first impression is very visual  and i see i really do see a nutshell and  then i see cats and dogs raining from  the sky and then i see joe being in a  can with its top off  and it really takes  some extra milliseconds or seconds of  that  computational power of the brain for me  to actually  arrive at a conclusion oh yeah so this  is an idiom and it means this and that  okay let's get to the next one so  this can really be an obstacle and so  you really might want to  think of that whenever you catch  yourself using some catchphrases or  idiomatic expressions especially when  they're spiked with  visual vocabulary  another way to make language easier is  to use very clear titles and summaries  other than a very quick overview which  we obviously cherish  it also provides context  so this is a fairly known  valuer known technique in journalism  this is called inverted pyramid writing  and it's often found in newspaper  articles you have a headline then you  have a quick summary and then you just  get to the article itself  so you also might want to think about  that  um  oh and i love this one uh yes list and  indices whenever possible whenever you  see the opportunity  uh try and itemize or list things  because  people would ask because we just love  lists we love lists of lists and lists  of how to organize lists and how to  organize lists of lists of lists and i  could go on and on so i'm just crazy  about organizing so just remember that  list  lists are made of absolute win for us  and that's really for the best  then  then  going further  whenever you have any sort of hyperlinks  or buttons  that say click me or click here  the first impression for users with  cognitive  issues  is  being an alice in wonderland and  just seeing all these imperatives  everywhere telling them to click here or  click there eat me drink me this is this  is absolutely terrible  what you might want to do is make the  links  really self-explanatory really telling  the user where they lead  and what's  what's behind the door  so instead of click me or click here for  more info  a better way to do this would be say  details of our return policy of go to  home page etc  so i'm careful with that now  when it comes to design itself  um obviously  high arousal websites are a horror to  look at  so this is an example of something that  you don't want to do  so  no flickering no super bright colors no  animations movements sounds um also be  fairly careful with contrast  um  you really might want to  use relatively high contrast but not too  high  so this is a very fine line so so  careful with that because  uh  because some some users might find  too high or too low contrast quite  daunting  so just  basically you don't want to do any  old-school late 90s design  um like geocities or angel fire um i  don't know how many of you here remember  geocities raise your hand  oh yes thank god  yeah so so you might remember this uh  all those animated uh gifs of  like flames or revolving skulls or  horizontal lines with like blood and  animated rainbows and marquis  god that was so terrible that was such a  dark age  of the internet  and and then came flash or the horror of  flash  so  so i'm really grateful that we are where  we are right now um  and then understandably uh try and avoid  patterns  uh because um  we might either get overwhelmed  by the patterns  or shut down so either stuck or  fascinated and you don't really want the  user to react in any of those two  extremes  um  branding is an interesting one which is  often overlooked  you should be very very careful whenever  you're designing a logo or putting any  sort of branding on your site or on your  product or in your app  because branding is very often  metaphorical  in a way that's 